WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.210
In 1979, trade unions in Britain
had 13.2 million members.

2
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:11.640
By 2025, about 6.6 million
UK employees were members.

3
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:17.110
On average, members earned 5.3 per
cent more an hour than non-members.

4
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.340
But when a union pushes pay up,

5
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.480
does someone pay with their job?

6
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.840
Can a group of workers win higher
pay without anyone losing theirs?

7
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.970
In this mission, you'll draw a
union wage on a job-market diagram,

8
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.480
step by step.

9
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.120
Then you'll judge which industries
a union can push hardest,

10
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.360
and why. Your mission: find out
whether higher pay must cost jobs.
